  "snapshot": "OrCAD-Altium-openscad",
  "instruction": "Complete the task using command-line or batch-capable tools from Altium Designer, OrCAD Capture, or OpenSCAD. The neutral schematic package `oscillator_core` is on the desktop. Add tolerance properties only to the required resistors. Requirements: - Write `oscillator_tolerance.edif`, `oscillator_tolerance.schematic.json`, and `component_properties.csv`. - `R42` must have `1%`; `R33`, `R39`, and `R34` must have `5%`. - Do not add tolerance to other components. [Software] Altium Designer is available at `D:\\Altium\\AD26\\X2.EXE`. OrCAD Capture is available at `D:\\orcad\\tools\\bin\\Capture.exe`. OpenSCAD is available as `openscad`.",
  "source": "https://www.altium.com/altium-designer; https://www.cadence.com/en_US/home/tools/pcb-design-and-analysis/orcad.html; https://openscad.org/; https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/OpenSCAD_User_Manual/Using_OpenSCAD_in_a_command_line_environment; https://www.ipc.org/ipc-2581",
